      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the Civil War, freed people founded the Fourth Ward, which survived until urban renewal razed it in the 1970s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.martinmariettacenter.com/art-collection/the-magic-of-the-fourth-ward",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1976, Charlotte declared Fourth Ward a historic district and launched Friends of Fourth Ward to preserve its legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://uptowncharlotte.com/post/hidden-history-in-fourth-ward",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Junior League restored the Berryhill House, then sold it to fund the preservation of nine other historic homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
